# Checked trace rows for the first pure kernel eight

The alternative generators 198, 1688 and 821 give the trace matrix as a product
of three displacement sums. Fourteen bounded packed-row products evaluate it;
every final row is one of the four specified plane vectors. Row 1 gives the
base vector and row 3 the second vector. This module certifies matrix arithmetic;
`TraceImage` connects it to the trace over the actual subgroup.

Source: the ATLAS tables and bit convention attributed in `KernelCount.Tables`
and `GeneratorCertificates.Packed`. Candidate rows are computed from those
unchanged tables by the discovery route in `FirstPureOvergroup/source/README.md`.
All arithmetic equalities below are checked by Lean's kernel.
-/

